{# The whole set, replaced in one move, or not at all.

   → POST /areas/{uuid}/zones/import → ZoneImportService::importFeatureCollection(), which parses
     through ZoneFeatureParser (a missing or repeated `name`, a non-polygon geometry) and rejects an
     overlap with ZoneOverlapException::betweenNames(). ONE transaction: a rejected file leaves the
     area exactly as it was.

   The design's per-feature verdict rows (✓ Karatu · valid · 237 km² — ✗ Eyasi · overlaps Naiyobi)
   are a PREVIEW of a file the server has parsed but not committed. The model layer ships no
   dry-run: importFeatureCollection() either writes the set or throws on the FIRST problem it meets.
   So what ships is that same message, verbatim, in the page's flash — which names the zone, the
   reason and (for an overlap) the zone it collided with — plus the all-or-nothing note that a
   single-message failure cannot say for itself. When a dry-run lands on the service, this panel
   grows the .vrow list and nothing else changes.

   "Draw a zone" is rendered and inert on purpose: it is the flow that comes later, and the app
   shows an unbuilt affordance rather than hiding it. It must not grow a route here. #}
<div class="c" id="import" data-w="import">
    <span class="tab"><span class="idx">PL·46</span>Import zones<span class="src">· GeoJSON FeatureCollection</span></span>

    {% if canManage %}
        <form method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data" data-zone-import
              action="{{ path('app_area_zones_import', {uuid: area.uuid}) }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('zone_manage') }}">
            <div class="dropz">
                {{ ux_icon('lucide:upload') }}
                <span class="filechip">One feature per zone · a <b>name</b> property on each · WGS84</span>
                <input type="file" name="zones" accept=".geojson,.json,application/geo+json,application/json"
                       class="fld" aria-label="Zones GeoJSON file" required>
                <button class="cta" type="submit">{{ ux_icon('lucide:upload') }}Import this file</button>
            </div>
        </form>
    {% else %}
        <div class="dropz">
            {{ ux_icon('lucide:upload') }}
            <span>Importing a zoning scheme is a manager's job. Ask one — or run it from a terminal.</span>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="allnone">
        {{ ux_icon('lucide:triangle-alert') }}
        <span><b>All-or-nothing.</b> If one feature fails validation — an overlap, a missing or repeated
            <b>name</b>, a geometry that is not a polygon — <b>nothing is imported</b> and the existing zones are
            untouched. Fix the source file and upload it again.</span>
    </div>

    <div class="rln" style="margin-top:12px;border-bottom:0">
        <span>Same import, from a terminal</span>
        <span class="mono d">app:zone:import {{ area.uuid }} zones.geojson</span>
    </div>

    {{ include('zones/_draw_soon.html.twig') }}
</div>
